WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.346 --> 00:00:01.582
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.582 --> 00:00:04.715
Today's message is live in the moment.

00:00:04.715 --> 00:00:06.341
Over to you, Misty Copeland.

00:00:06.341 --> 00:00:08.593
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.593 --> 00:00:11.274
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.274 --> 00:00:13.964
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:13.964 --> 00:00:18.072
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.072 --> 00:00:20.314
- I think that when I was
younger, I was just, you know,

00:00:20.314 --> 00:00:23.914
you get so like, antsy, and
you just want the good things

00:00:23.914 --> 00:00:27.233
to come, and it's hard to
enjoy the process, and I think

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:28.701
that's something that I really

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:30.673
understand and appreciate now.

00:00:30.673 --> 00:00:34.048
I mean, my life is so
chaotic with just being busy

00:00:34.048 --> 00:00:36.195
all the time, that I
literally just take everything

00:00:36.195 --> 00:00:37.851
one step at a time.

00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:39.995
Like, even when I'm on the stage,

00:00:39.995 --> 00:00:42.665
and I'm like, I can't
think about third act,

00:00:42.665 --> 00:00:44.996
I'm in second act now and
I'm going to think about

00:00:44.996 --> 00:00:46.706
the pique arabesque I'm about to do,

00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:49.043
not about the, you know, the,

00:00:49.043 --> 00:00:51.338
the pirouettes I'm going
to do in two seconds.

00:00:51.338 --> 00:00:54.659
So it's literally just
like, taking everything,

00:00:54.659 --> 00:00:57.647
you know, just pacing yourself
in one thing at a time.

00:00:57.647 --> 00:00:59.618
- If you can't learn to
appreciate the moment,

00:00:59.618 --> 00:01:00.777
you'll never be happy.

00:01:00.777 --> 00:01:02.542
I think one of the things
that we, as entrepreneurs,

00:01:02.542 --> 00:01:05.853
are great at, is being
frustrated with the status quo,

00:01:05.853 --> 00:01:07.862
is wanting more, it's
wanting to change something,

00:01:07.862 --> 00:01:09.824
wanting to change the
way an industry is done,

00:01:09.824 --> 00:01:11.184
because we're so angry and frustrated

00:01:11.184 --> 00:01:12.658
with how it's currently being done.

00:01:12.658 --> 00:01:13.971
And that's great, and that's a strength,

00:01:13.971 --> 00:01:15.813
and that's a tool, and
we should lean in on it.

00:01:15.813 --> 00:01:17.514
At the same time though,

00:01:17.514 --> 00:01:20.368
I want you to be grateful
for what you do have,

00:01:20.368 --> 00:01:22.882
to recognize the abundance
of opportunities and wealth

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.239
that you have already living.

00:01:24.239 --> 00:01:27.056
The fact that you are living,
and watching this video,

00:01:27.056 --> 00:01:29.676
and have access to YouTube, puts you ahead

00:01:29.676 --> 00:01:31.337
of, still, most of the world.

00:01:31.337 --> 00:01:34.162
And, recognizing that, and
being so grateful that if,

00:01:34.162 --> 00:01:37.271
even if you never accomplish
any more of your goals,

00:01:37.271 --> 00:01:39.360
that you have an amazing life.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.483
I think it's helpful.

00:01:40.483 --> 00:01:42.590
Now, I don't think it's,
only focus on how great

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.061
everything is, 'cause then,
you don't do anything else.

00:01:45.061 --> 00:01:46.472
Right, you don't want to change things.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.408
That little bit of frustration is good,

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:49.986
but I think you need both;
I think too many people

00:01:49.986 --> 00:01:53.542
don't lean too hard, on the
negative, on the frustration,

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:55.372
on the way things are currently done, and

00:01:55.372 --> 00:01:57.840
if that's all you are chasing,
then you'll never be happy.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.043
There's a great story from
Thich Nhat Hanh, where

00:02:00.043 --> 00:02:02.593
he's talking about washing
the dishes to wash the dishes.

00:02:02.593 --> 00:02:05.445
He's doing this retreat with his students,

00:02:05.445 --> 00:02:06.796
and at the end of every
night, they would go over

00:02:06.796 --> 00:02:09.444
to his place, and he
would make them dinner,

00:02:09.444 --> 00:02:11.152
and then he would wash the plates.

00:02:11.152 --> 00:02:14.315
And, one of the guys
who came to his session

00:02:14.315 --> 00:02:15.720
said, hey, let me wash the plates for you.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.057
You did a lot of work, you helped us out,

00:02:17.057 --> 00:02:19.718
you fed us, how about I
wash the plates for you.

00:02:19.718 --> 00:02:22.601
And he told them that, if
you're going to wash the plates,

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.115
then you need to wash the plates.

00:02:24.115 --> 00:02:25.997
You wash the plates to wash the plates,

00:02:25.997 --> 00:02:28.236
and what that means is, so many times,

00:02:28.236 --> 00:02:30.323
when people are washing the
plates, what are you doing?

00:02:30.323 --> 00:02:31.819
You're thinking of what's next,

00:02:31.819 --> 00:02:33.914
and you're not actually
focused on washing the plates.

00:02:33.914 --> 00:02:35.944
You're thinking about the
conversations you're going to have

00:02:35.944 --> 00:02:38.505
after you finish washing the dishes.

00:02:38.505 --> 00:02:40.209
And then, when you're having
the conversations after,

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:41.265
you're thinking about
what you're going to do

00:02:41.265 --> 00:02:42.293
later on that night.

00:02:42.293 --> 00:02:43.919
And when you're actually
doing that thing, later on

00:02:43.919 --> 00:02:44.752
that night, you're thinking about

00:02:44.752 --> 00:02:45.687
what's going to happen tomorrow.

00:02:45.687 --> 00:02:48.576
We're so focused on always
thinking about what's next,

00:02:48.576 --> 00:02:50.525
that we don't take the time to enjoy

00:02:50.525 --> 00:02:51.882
what's happening right now.

00:02:51.882 --> 00:02:54.361
I'm enjoying making this
video for you right now.

00:02:54.361 --> 00:02:56.194
I'm entirely focused on
just making this video.

00:02:56.194 --> 00:02:57.883
I'm not thinking about the next
video that I'm going to do.

00:02:57.883 --> 00:02:59.933
I'm not thinking about how
I'm going to spend my evening.

00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:02.351
I'm here, trying to be
with you, in this moment.

00:03:02.351 --> 00:03:05.609
And the more time you can
spend being in the moment,

00:03:05.609 --> 00:03:08.157
it helps you be a happier
and healthier entrepreneur.

00:03:08.157 --> 00:03:10.989
I think, too often, we're
focused just on thinking about

00:03:10.989 --> 00:03:13.908
what's happening next, and we
don't actually get to spend

00:03:13.908 --> 00:03:16.392
time enjoying our family,
enjoying our customers,

00:03:16.392 --> 00:03:18.543
enjoying the work and the
process that we're doing.

00:03:18.543 --> 00:03:22.714
So if you can take all of
that, and learn to be present,

00:03:22.714 --> 00:03:25.124
and yes, focus on the frustrations,

00:03:25.124 --> 00:03:26.607
so that it helps you become
a better entrepreneur,

00:03:26.607 --> 00:03:28.262
but at the same time, be grateful,

00:03:28.262 --> 00:03:30.642
and mindful in the moment, for
everything that you do have.

00:03:30.642 --> 00:03:32.520
I think it'll make you happier, healthier,

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.346
and a more successful entrepreneur.

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:35.890
So the question of the day
today, is, I'm curious,

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:38.445
what do you do to be
present, in the moment?

00:03:38.445 --> 00:03:40.720
Curious to find out, leave
it in the comments below.

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.575
I also want to give a
quick shout-out to Peter.

00:03:42.575 --> 00:03:44.765
Peter, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:03:44.765 --> 00:03:47.020
Your One Word, it really,
really means a lot to me, man,

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.479
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:48.479 --> 00:03:50.069
So thank you guys again, for watching.

00:03:50.069 --> 00:03:51.123
I believe in you.

00:03:51.123 --> 00:03:53.013
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:03:53.013 --> 00:03:54.809
and whatever your one word is.

00:03:54.809 --> 00:03:57.350
Much love, and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning,

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.661
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:03:59.661 --> 00:04:02.470
♫ I wake up every morning

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.887
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:04:07.678 --> 00:04:09.443
- A Head Full of Dreams,
the tour is going on now,

00:04:09.443 --> 00:04:11.494
you just got off the South American line.

00:04:11.494 --> 00:04:14.787
I mean, the crowds, the show,

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.488
does it ever, how do you keep it fresh?

00:04:17.488 --> 00:04:19.039
Because, it's not your first rodeo,

00:04:19.039 --> 00:04:21.353
it's your thousands,
ten-thousands, I mean,

00:04:21.353 --> 00:04:22.525
you've been doing it.

00:04:22.525 --> 00:04:24.358
- Well, here's how we keep it fresh:

00:04:24.358 --> 00:04:26.031
Bruce Springsteen,
apparently, I don't know

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:28.136
if he really does or not, used to say

00:04:28.136 --> 00:04:30.205
to the rest of the E Street Band,

00:04:30.205 --> 00:04:31.641
this could be someone's first show

00:04:31.641 --> 00:04:33.059
and it could be someone's last show.

00:04:33.059 --> 00:04:34.789
So, let's treat it like that.

00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:37.623
So, I have that inspiration, and then

00:04:37.623 --> 00:04:40.307
some other things in my
life, that just make me,

00:04:40.307 --> 00:04:42.659
every time, before we go on
stage, I really think about

00:04:42.659 --> 00:04:44.531
like, who's showed up, how
much they've been through

00:04:44.531 --> 00:04:46.907
to get there, and,

00:04:46.907 --> 00:04:49.496
also for us, at the moment,
we're just so into it.

00:04:49.496 --> 00:04:51.358
We took a break from
touring, on the last album

00:04:51.358 --> 00:04:53.942
we did, called Ghost
Stories, so we're so excited

00:04:53.942 --> 00:04:57.332
to be there, and we know
that nothing lasts forever,

00:04:57.332 --> 00:04:58.768
so I think that we're just really,

00:04:58.768 --> 00:05:00.584
more than ever, living in the moment,

00:05:00.584 --> 00:05:03.291
and trying to appreciate the fact that,

00:05:03.291 --> 00:05:04.567
for some people, it's their first show,

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:05.996
and some people, you know, you know.

00:05:05.996 --> 00:05:07.561
- And, that has to be a perspective that,

00:05:07.561 --> 00:05:08.780
that's not immediate, right?

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:09.897
You learn that perspective.
- You have to work

00:05:09.897 --> 00:05:11.322
to that perspective.
- Yeah.

00:05:11.322 --> 00:05:13.221
- We definitely went through
a period, about 10 years ago,

00:05:13.221 --> 00:05:15.040
of feeling like, what are we doing?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.844
You know, questioning
everything, and not really

00:05:16.844 --> 00:05:19.175
able to take in the joy of it.

00:05:19.175 --> 00:05:21.447
- [Interviewer] That must have been hard.

00:05:21.447 --> 00:05:23.650
- I mean, everything's in
perspective, but for us,

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:26.586
as a band, it was a bit hard,
like, what are we, you know.

00:05:26.586 --> 00:05:29.588
But, slowly, just, you keep
going, and you find great people

00:05:29.588 --> 00:05:32.138
who come in and help you
out, and teach you things.

00:05:32.138 --> 00:05:35.929
And I think, the more that you let in,

00:05:35.929 --> 00:05:37.857
it's very easy right
now, with social media,

00:05:37.857 --> 00:05:39.615
to let in anything negative, you know.

00:05:39.615 --> 00:05:42.552
Whatever you do, someone is
going to slag it off, online.

00:05:42.552 --> 00:05:44.359
- Well, you're not on social media at all.

00:05:44.359 --> 00:05:45.820
- Personally, we are as a band.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.221
I don't really personally do it.

00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:48.912
I'm not that good at selfies.

00:05:48.912 --> 00:05:49.866
(laughing)

00:05:49.866 --> 00:05:50.957
- That's the honest answer.
- That's the reason.

00:05:50.957 --> 00:05:51.790
- Yeah.

00:05:53.647 --> 00:05:56.033
So I made a decision that, well, you know,

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:57.175
it's easy to take in the bad stuff,

00:05:57.175 --> 00:05:59.633
so I'm going to really
take in the good stuff, and

00:05:59.633 --> 00:06:01.409
appreciate, these people have shown up,

00:06:01.409 --> 00:06:04.414
and they want to sing
our songs together, and

00:06:04.414 --> 00:06:06.303
that's great, I'm into it.

00:06:06.303 --> 00:06:08.324
- It can't ever get old.
- So it's very fresh.

00:06:08.324 --> 00:06:09.157
It never gets old.

00:06:09.157 --> 00:06:10.550
That's the thing, it never gets old.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.785
- You're not meant to
put a goal on your life.

00:06:12.785 --> 00:06:16.442
You're not meant to say, once
I get there, I'll have it all.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:19.671
I think that that's the biggest
lesson I've needed to learn,

00:06:19.671 --> 00:06:21.476
is how to be present, in that moment,

00:06:21.476 --> 00:06:24.054
and to know that I'm always
going to strive for something.

00:06:24.054 --> 00:06:26.240
I think everybody who's watched my story,

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.250
they've seen that not
everything has kind of been

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.479
handed to me, and I've been
honest about everything.

00:06:32.479 --> 00:06:35.436
Some of the things that
haven't been me, in the past,

00:06:35.436 --> 00:06:37.837
and other things, I've
been so passionate about,

00:06:37.837 --> 00:06:39.065
and so spot-on with.

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:42.723
So, if anything, that's
what Revival represents.

00:06:42.723 --> 00:06:47.322
It's that, I feel the most
confident I've ever felt,

00:06:47.322 --> 00:06:49.524
and it goes like that.
(laughing)

00:06:49.524 --> 00:06:52.653
It's like, it's constantly changing,

00:06:52.653 --> 00:06:55.006
and I don't know, I think that's just,

00:06:55.006 --> 00:06:56.499
that's what I want it to feel like.

00:06:56.499 --> 00:06:58.152
- Your background is
fairly well documented,

00:06:58.152 --> 00:07:00.851
the things you went through,
which have shaped you.

00:07:00.851 --> 00:07:02.839
How much of that is really behind you?

00:07:02.839 --> 00:07:04.814
How much do those ghosts still haunt you?

00:07:04.814 --> 00:07:08.320
The involvement in, you know,
issues that got you in prison,

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:12.487
and tortured, and, you know,
the drug use, and so on.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.192
- I am myself, and my circumstance.

00:07:17.192 --> 00:07:21.158
I think that, like a Spanish philosopher,

00:07:21.158 --> 00:07:24.328
used to say, so, who am I?

00:07:24.328 --> 00:07:28.060
I'm a sum of all the experience
that I lived, in my life.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:30.617
That said, of course, I don't look back,

00:07:30.617 --> 00:07:32.195
because if I look back,

00:07:32.195 --> 00:07:35.445
I may become a start of salt.

00:07:36.714 --> 00:07:38.358
So I try to live my life here,

00:07:38.358 --> 00:07:41.447
but it is the sum of difficult moments,

00:07:41.447 --> 00:07:45.352
good moments, experiences
that I had in my life,

00:07:45.352 --> 00:07:48.546
that brought me here,
in front of this camera,

00:07:48.546 --> 00:07:49.796
talking to you.

00:07:50.641 --> 00:07:54.960
You don't live your life,
in this capitalistic sense,

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.608
that to accumulate knowledge,
as you accumulate money.

00:07:58.608 --> 00:08:00.330
No, no, no, no, no.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.209
Life is about the present moment.

00:08:03.209 --> 00:08:05.712
And, you're here, you're here now,

00:08:05.712 --> 00:08:08.584
and then you have an
idea, or have something,

00:08:08.584 --> 00:08:12.768
but that may be a root in your past,

00:08:12.768 --> 00:08:15.435
but you don't know, so what I try to do,

00:08:15.435 --> 00:08:19.225
is to live my life as full,
as intensely, as I can.

